1. SELENE (KAGUYA) lunar limb profile — moon/limb/kaguya_lalt.bin
================================================================================

Source data
  SELENE Global Grid Topographic Data of the Moon (LALT_GGT_NUM), dataset
  sln-l-lalt-5-topo-ggt-num-v2.0, version 2.0, published 2017.
  Origin of the data: ISAS/JAXA.
  Provided by the SELENE (KAGUYA) Data Archive (DARTS), ISAS/JAXA:
    https://darts.isas.jaxa.jp/datasets/darts:sln-l-lalt-5-topo-ggt-num-v2.0
    https://data.darts.isas.jaxa.jp/pub/pds3/sln-l-lalt-5-topo-ggt-num-v2.0/

Acknowledgement, as requested by the SELENE Data Archive
  "We thank the SELENE(KAGUYA) LALT team and the SELENE Data Archive for
   providing the SELENE(KAGUYA) data. SELENE is a Japanese mission developed
   and operated by JAXA."

Modifications
  The original PDS3 fixed-width table (1/16 degree global grid, 2880 x 5760
  samples) was converted to a float32 elevation grid and then resampled into a
  limb-radius profile table: the limb height is tabulated on a 1 degree grid of
  selenographic (libration) longitude and latitude and on a 0.1 degree grid of
  position angle, taking max (R + h) cos(alpha) over a +/-9 degree arc for each
  direction. Values are quantized to 4 m, delta-encoded along longitude and
  latitude, and then stored in this project's own zlib-compressed LLB1
  container. No other changes were made.

Licence
