2. Planetary and lunar theories — planet/internal/semianalytic/**/*.bin
================================================================================

Upstream theories and authors
  VSOP2013 — planetary theory, Simon, Francou, Fienga & Manche (2013),
  distributed by IMCCE at https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/planets/vsop2013/
  TOP2013 — planetary theory for the outer planets, IMCCE, distributed at
  https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/planets/top2013/
  ELP/MPP02 — lunar theory, J. Chapront, M. Chapront & G. Francou, 2003,
  distributed by SYRTE, Observatoire de Paris (not through IMCCE's ftp server)
  at ftp://cyrano-se.obspm.fr/pub/2_lunar_solutions/2_elpmpp02/
  Its distribution README.TXT (December 2002) is purely scientific — authors,
  description, file list and references — and states no licence and no terms
  of use.
  Used by the legacy model as well:
  ELP2000-82B — earlier lunar solution, Chapront-Touzé & Chapront, distributed
  by IMCCE at https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/moon/elp82b/
  VSOP87 — earlier planetary series, Bretagnon & Francou (1988).

What this project distributes
  Its own numerical refits of those theories' argument structure to the JPL
  DE440/DE441 ephemerides. The amplitudes in the *.bin tables are produced by
  this project's fitting pipeline; the upstream coefficient files are not
  redistributed here. Relative to the upstream theories the tables are
  modified in two ways: (1) the argument structure is truncated to the terms
  the fit retains, and (2) every amplitude is re-fitted to DE440/DE441 instead
  of being taken from the published series.

Published constants
  The argument phases and frequencies (the VSOP2013 "ll(1..17)" set) and the
  GM constants used by the generator are published in the VSOP2013 README.pdf
  distributed by IMCCE and in Simon, Francou, Fienga & Manche, A&A 557, A49
  (2013); for the Moon, in Chapront & Francou, A&A 404, 735 (2003).

Rights in the underlying theories
  This project can neither allow nor forbid the use of the VSOP2013, TOP2013,
  ELP/MPP02, ELP2000-82B or VSOP87 theories. Apache-2.0 covers only this
  project's own work — its code, and its compilation and rearrangement of the
  published series — and not the theories themselves. Downstream users who
  need to rely on the terms of the underlying theories should consult the IMCCE
  legal notice,
    https://www.imcce.fr/mentions-legales
  which restricts reproduction and makes commercial or professional use
  subject to IMCCE authorisation.

ELP/MPP02 terms
  The official ELP/MPP02 distribution ships README.TXT (December 2002) and the
  explanatory note elpmpp02.pdf; neither states a licence or terms of use, and
  no separate terms file is included. This project therefore treats ELP/MPP02
  as carrying no stated terms and relies on the disclaimer under "Rights in
  the underlying theories" above. Note also that IMCCE's ftp server carries
  only ELP2000-82B, not ELP/MPP02. Downstream users who need a formal position
  should consult SYRTE, https://syrte.obspm.fr/, and the IMCCE legal notice.

